          {
            "title": "Intro",
            "id": 82502,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Per esplorare i dati che memorizziamo nelle liste, è spesso utile trovare i valori estremi: il minimo e il massimo.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"light_intensity = [\" /><text value=\"200\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"500\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"60\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"90\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /></content></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Maximum",
            "id": 82503,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Per trovare il numero più grande in un elenco di dati come <code>scores</code>, scrivi <code>max()</code>, con il nome dell'elenco tra parentesi.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"scores = [\" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(max(scores))\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"29\" endIndex=\"32\" /><option startIndex=\"32\" endIndex=\"33\" /><option startIndex=\"39\" endIndex=\"40\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"12\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>max</code>, seguito da <code>(</code> e infine <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Per trovare il numero più grande in una lista, usa <code>max()</code> con il nome della lista tra parentesi.</p><p>La lista <code>scores</code> contiene quattro numeri. Fai stampare al codice quello più grande, <code>12</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"scores = [\" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(max(scores))\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"29\" endIndex=\"32\" /><option startIndex=\"32\" endIndex=\"33\" /><option startIndex=\"33\" endIndex=\"39\" /><option startIndex=\"39\" endIndex=\"40\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"min\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;scores&quot;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"scores[0]\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"12\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>max</code>, seguito da <code>(</code>, <code>scores</code> e infine <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Minimum",
            "id": 82504,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Per trovare il numero più piccolo nell'elenco <code>scores</code>, usiamo <code>min()</code> con il nome dell'elenco tra parentesi.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"scores = [\" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(min(scores))\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"29\" endIndex=\"32\" /><option startIndex=\"33\" endIndex=\"39\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"max\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"1\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>min</code>, seguito da <code>scores</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Save in variable",
            "id": 82505,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Possiamo riutilizzare i risultati di <code>min()</code> e <code>max()</code> salvandoli in variabili.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"scores = [\" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"min_score = min(scores)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"max_score = max(scores)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(max_score)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(min_score)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"33\" endIndex=\"34\" /><option startIndex=\"35\" endIndex=\"46\" /><option startIndex=\"57\" endIndex=\"58\" /><option startIndex=\"59\" endIndex=\"70\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"12\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"1\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>=</code>, seguito da <code>min(scores)</code> e poi <code>=</code>, <code>max(scores)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Salva il minimo in <code>min_score</code> e il massimo in <code>max_score</code>. Stampa prima il massimo, così l'output sarà <code>12</code> e poi <code>1</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"scores = [\" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"min_score = min(scores)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"max_score = max(scores)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(max_score)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(min_score)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"35\" endIndex=\"46\" /><option startIndex=\"59\" endIndex=\"70\" /><option startIndex=\"78\" endIndex=\"87\" /><option startIndex=\"95\" endIndex=\"104\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"12\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"1\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>min(scores)</code>, seguito da <code>max(scores)</code>, <code>max_score</code> e infine <code>min_score</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Maximum ",
            "id": 82605,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Che cosa fa <code>max()</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Trova il valore più grande in un elenco di numeri</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Restituisce la lunghezza di un elenco di numeri</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Trova il valore più grande in un elenco di numeri.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>La funzione <code>max()</code> trova il valore maggiore in una lista di numeri.</p><p>La lista è <code>prices = [12, 18, 9]</code>. Che cosa restituisce <code>max(prices)</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>18</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>3</code>, perché la lista contiene tre valori</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>9</code>, perché è il valore finale</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>18</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Minimum",
            "id": 82606,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A cosa serve <code>min()</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Trovare il numero più piccolo in un elenco</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Rimozione di elementi da un elenco</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Trovare il numero più piccolo in un elenco.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>La funzione <code>min()</code> trova il numero più piccolo di una lista.</p><p>Un programma richiede il valore più basso in <code>temperatures</code>, ma usa <code>max(temperatures)</code>. Quale sostituzione lo corregge?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>min(temperatures)</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>len(temperatures)</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>temperatures[0]</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>min(temperatures)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Save in variable",
            "id": 82607,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Come possiamo riutilizzare il valore restituito da <code>max(jeans_sizes)</code>?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"jeans_sizes = [\" /><text value=\"25\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"28\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"40\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"max(jeans_sizes)\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Salvando il risultato di <code>max(jeans_sizes)</code> in una variabile</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Non possiamo riutilizzare il valore, possiamo solo visualizzarlo una volta</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Salvando il risultato di <code>max(jeans_sizes)</code> in una variabile.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Possiamo riutilizzare il valore di <code>max(jeans_sizes)</code> salvandone il risultato in una variabile.</p><p>Quale riga sostituisce l'ultima e memorizza il risultato in <code>largest_size</code>?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"jeans_sizes = [\" /><text value=\"25\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"28\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"40\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"max(jeans_sizes)\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>largest_size = max(jeans_sizes)</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>largest_size == max(jeans_sizes)</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>largest_size = jeans_sizes</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>largest_size = max(jeans_sizes)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Maximum",
            "id": 82608,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Trova la temperatura più alta degli ultimi tre giorni con <code>max()</code>, nella lista <code>temperatures</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"temperatures = [\" /><text value=\"68\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"60\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"81\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(max(temperatures))\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"34\" endIndex=\"37\" /><option startIndex=\"37\" endIndex=\"38\" /><option startIndex=\"38\" endIndex=\"50\" /><option startIndex=\"50\" endIndex=\"51\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"81\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>max</code>, seguito da <code>(</code> e poi <code>temperatures</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>La lista <code>temperatures</code> contiene gli ultimi tre giorni. Fai stampare al codice la temperatura più alta, <code>81</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"temperatures = [\" /><text value=\"68\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"60\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"81\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(max(temperatures))\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"34\" endIndex=\"37\" /><option startIndex=\"37\" endIndex=\"38\" /><option startIndex=\"38\" endIndex=\"50\" /><option startIndex=\"50\" endIndex=\"51\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"min\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"scores\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"68\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"81\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>max</code>, seguito da <code>(</code>, <code>temperatures</code> e infine <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
